  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PPP reflections</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This assignment analyses the public&#x2013;private partnerships (PPPs) implemented under the Sustainable Water Fund (FDW) programme to better understand how partnership structures contribute to water security objectives in developing countries. The study reviews the characteristics of partnerships across the FDW portfolio, identifies lessons learned, best practices and challenges in PPP cooperation, and provides insights for policymakers and project implementers on how partnerships can support sustainability, scaling and inclusive outcomes in water-related interventions.</narrative>
  </description>
